1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
In a food-production facility, a fan can report running while exhaust remains below the
configured target. Open Soom connects that difference to an actionable, traceable response.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Device adapters publish a common observation contract to a real one M two M platform.
Discovery, subscriptions, group queries, and access policies support one shared operating path.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The dashboard keeps every zone visible. This recorded interactive demo starts with a cooking-
line fault, sends a permitted damper command, and then displays the observed recovery.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The same tools are available through a Codex plugin and a standalone model runner. Here, real
model-generated calls discover equipment, inspect evidence, request action, and verify the
result.

5
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:04,000
A command is only the beginning. The device must acknowledge it. Two fresh later observations
must meet the facility profile before open Soom records a verified recovery.

6
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:17,000
When the damper opens but airflow does not recover, the incident stays unresolved. An
acknowledgement never becomes a success claim. The evidence remains available for follow-up.

7
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Food production is one reference profile. A learning facility and a second vendor format use
the same core, with their own targets, units, and permitted controls.

8
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Open source means easier adoption. Replay the local demo, use Codex workflows, and inspect the
evidence.

9
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Open Soom. Real software. Virtual equipment. Open-source air operations. Explore the code.
